/**
@page page_exagrype_foccz4 First-order CCZ4

There are two flavours of the CCZ4 solver. @ref exagrype.api.FOCCZ4Solver
evolves all 59 unknowns of the first-order formulation.
@ref exagrype.api.FOSOCCZ4Solver evolves the 25 primary unknowns only, and its
partner @ref exagrype.api.FOSOReconstructionSolver recomputes the 34 first
derivatives from them in front of each Runge-Kutta stage. Both share all CCZ4
kernels via @ref exagrype.api.CCZ4SolverBase. The design, status and lab notes
of the second flavour are collected on
@subpage page_exagrype_fo_so_project_plan "this page".


@section page_exagrype_foccz4_ordering Ordering of the unknowns

The 59 entries of the first-order formulation are stored in the order of
exagrype.api.FOCCZ4Solver.Unknowns, i.e. consecutively in memory per
volume. Symmetric tensors (@f$ \tilde\gamma_{ij}, \tilde A_{ij} @f$) hold
their six independent components in the order xx, xy, xz, yy, yz, zz. The
derivative blocks hold the derivative in the direction named in the label
(x, y, z) in front of the remaining tensor index.
The last column states whether @ref exagrype.api.FOSOCCZ4Solver evolves the
entry (primary) or whether @ref exagrype.api.FOSOReconstructionSolver recomputes it.

| Name     | Entries | Index range | Meaning                                              | FOSO    |
|----------|---------|-------------|------------------------------------------------------|---------|
| G        | 6       | 0-5         | conformal metric @f$ \tilde\gamma_{ij} @f$          | primary |
| K        | 6       | 6-11        | trace-free extrinsic curvature @f$ \tilde A_{ij} @f$ | primary |
| theta    | 1       | 12          | Z4 constraint damping variable @f$ \Theta @f$        | primary |
| Z        | 3       | 13-15       | conformal connection @f$ \hat\Gamma^i @f$           | primary |
| lapse    | 1       | 16          | lapse @f$ \alpha @f$                                 | primary |
| shift    | 3       | 17-19       | shift @f$ \beta^i @f$                                | primary |
| b        | 3       | 20-22       | Gamma-driver auxiliary @f$ b^i @f$                   | primary |
| traceK   | 1       | 23          | trace of extrinsic curvature @f$ K @f$               | primary |
| phi      | 1       | 24          | conformal factor @f$ \phi @f$                        | primary |
| dLapse   | 3       | 25-27       | @f$ \partial_i \alpha @f$ (auxiliary @f$ A_i @f$)    | derived |
| dxShift  | 3       | 28-30       | @f$ \partial_x \beta^i @f$                          | derived |
| dyShift  | 3       | 31-33       | @f$ \partial_y \beta^i @f$                          | derived |
| dzShift  | 3       | 34-36       | @f$ \partial_z \beta^i @f$                          | derived |
| dxG      | 6       | 37-42       | @f$ \partial_x \tilde\gamma_{ij} @f$               | derived |
| dyG      | 6       | 43-48       | @f$ \partial_y \tilde\gamma_{ij} @f$               | derived |
| dzG      | 6       | 49-54       | @f$ \partial_z \tilde\gamma_{ij} @f$               | derived |
| P        | 3       | 55-57       | @f$ P_i @f$ (derivative of the conformal factor)     | derived |
| K0       | 1       | 58          | initial trace of extrinsic curvature; does not evolve | derived |

Primary entries sum to 25, derived ones to 34.


 */
 